  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the key uncertainty is whether a multimodal + multiprofile pipeline can outperform simpler baselines, and which component choices are most impactful. Config_006 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA-2000, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) tests the full multimodal hypothesis using well-established, low-risk components: PCA is fast and reliable (no encoder training), ResNet50 is a standard and lighter image backbone, avgpool is a robust aggregation, and concat is the simplest fusion. This establishes a meaningful 'standard multimodal' baseline. If it performs well, subsequent experiments can upgrade individual components (ViT-L, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion, scGPT/scVI encoders) to exploit the promising direction. If it underperforms, we learn whether the issue is multimodal fusion itself, the multiprofile aggregation, or the encoder choices—guiding a pivot toward unimodal baselines or simpler configurations. This maximizes information gain for the remaining 9 experiments."
}

